          {"id": "b", "text": "$a\\sqrt3=\\sqrt{3a^2}$ for $a\\geq0$, and $a\\sqrt3=\\sqrt{3a^2}$ for $a<0$.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$x\\sqrt{\\frac2x}=\\sqrt{2x}$ on $x>0$, and $x\\sqrt{-\\frac2x}=-\\sqrt{-2x}$ on $x<0$.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$x\\sqrt{\\frac2x}=\\sqrt{2x}$ on $x>0$, and $x\\sqrt{-\\frac2x}=\\sqrt{-2x}$ on $x<0$.", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Move all four monomials inside with the correct sign and preserve the implicit nonzero domains in the last two.",
        "source_solution": "Full 828 a-d: sqrt(3a^2) on a>=0; -sqrt(3a^2) on a<0; sqrt(2x) on x>0; -sqrt(-2x) on x<0. The two fractions exclude x=0 and force opposite signs of x.",
        "unit_reason": "One multiple question pairs explicit-sign and implicitly determined-sign rewrites. Neither a domain endpoint nor a minus sign becomes a separate trivial answer slot.",
